oMLX
----
Parts of MFQ's Metal scheduling and model-specific kernels are adapted from
oMLX, with MFQ-specific model layouts and runtime integration.

Copyright (c) 2026 Apple Inc.
License: Apache License 2.0 (`LICENSE`)
Source: https://github.com/jundot/omlx

The balanced memory-budget and release-credit accounting follow
omlx/process_memory_enforcer.py, adapted to MFQ's managed runtime processes.

The Flash-Next grouped decode-submission policy is adapted from oMLX's
Qwen4 eager dispatch in language.py at revision
87460f4d50de79aef9b67e99e215c31f0a89b445, with MFQ-specific single-token and
component-profiling guards.
The singleton selected-block GQA gather/SDPA path follows
contiguous_causal_gathered_qsa_decode in qsa_fast.py at the same revision;
MFQ fuses K/V gathering and retains a validity mask for invalid block IDs.
The single-token Gated DeltaNet step layout follows
qwen4_decode_step_fused in qwen35_gdn_prework.py at revision
107e271ad449e2a9a060ec9a76d0c1d42724a2e2; MFQ retains its FP32 recurrent
state, transposed cache contract, and existing reduction order.
The Qwen4 QSA prefill pipeline, fused indexer-score and chronological FP32
top-k kernels follow qsa_fast.py, language.py and the native DSA indexer at
revision a435a3736071286fdb2b74f486b3505f23f3c194. The sparse main kernels
adapt its NAX half2 and tiled GQA paths; MFQ retains its quantized projections
and cache interfaces. MFQ's prefill-only NAX variant packs a single FP16
probability term and uses a two-barrier score exchange, retaining FP32 scores,
softmax and accumulation.
The shared non-Dspark MTP depth controller, performance handoff, retry policy
and cross-request timing estimates are adapted from batch_generator.py at
revision a435a3736071286fdb2b74f486b3505f23f3c194, translated to C++ for
MFQ\'s Metal and CUDA generation engines.
Copyright 2025 oMLX contributors
License: Apache License 2.0 (`LICENSE`)

